Question 1) "During the attacker's port scan, what is the highest-numbered TCP port that responded as open on the victim host? (Hint: in a SYN scan, the victim's SYN-ACK source port is the open port.)"
-------------------


This is a case of Filtering for Syn-Ack responses (second TCP handshake response) to the attackers TCP port scan in Wireshark. I used the filter -->

tcp.flags.syn == 1 && tcp.flags.ack == 1

This pulls all packets containing both the SYN and ACK flags. 

From here you can click the Info header which orders the packets in Ascending order by port number.

At this point, you can identify the Highest Port number as 3306.


